|term[location] :status settled :defined-by def-locations-and-paths :anchor identity-vs-location
  :word location
  :avoid [place address]
  A containment claim over a designated container — "contained in c", where c is named by a [[term/containment-coordinate]].
  |invariants
    - Is a kind of [[term/description]] — the owned description ([[DECISIONS#d12-location-is-description|D12 location-is-description]])
    - Names its container via one or more [[term/containment-coordinate]]
    - Composes with other locations by subset-nesting
    - Resolution is delegable: the container's community can enumerate and route
  |note :audience maintainer
    "Standing alone, a location is a scope" — scope mint proposed, NOT ratified; do not cite it as a term.
